  "observations": [
    "Final list run 16 passes 111 rows and 26 complete native images at actual 1x/2x. Real seat reference keys and pointer input match native state, full-width selected/key identities and action counts. Cases include single/multiple selection, Shift navigation and click, disabled rows, original scrollbar and wheel input, native clipping/scroll position, empty models, unchanged native cell/key context, callback lifetime guards, duplicate/invalid-UTF8/unknown-key/unknown-flag/single-mode rejection and whole images.",
    "Fresh-state capture run 15 independently passes 109/26. Run 16 additionally proves the actual older 528-byte client and loader work with the new provider. Its actual older provider reports new list methods unsupported. The unchanged 528-byte prefix is checked by a compiled offsetof assertion; runtime table readback is version 1/568.",
    "Current native matrix regression passes 312 rows/34 full images and popup-title regression 88/16. Scoped total: 511 rows/76 images, with the separate 109/26 capture repeat and the full existing NativeUI provider/transport regression recorded separately.",
    "The first test initializes NSBrowser class metadata before NSApplication/backend setup and aborts at font enumeration. Later tests bootstrap through the provider first. Early pointer-reference injection fails because the original native tracking loop reads actual pointer position; final references use real seat input instead.",
    "Reusing the ordinary reference window as an image oracle intermittently composites an unselected focus-row title over its previous glyphs after Shift navigation. Capture-order/focus-settle/freezing attempts can pass individual runs but do not remove that history-dependent reference damage. Final input comparison keeps that original reference; final paint comparison uses a fresh ordinary native list populated from its resulting native state. Original native drawing remains unchanged and pixels require exact equality. Failed test snapshots/runs are retained.",
    "The first provider blocks all pointer input when rows are disabled; the final shared gate permits list hit testing so the original native scroller remains usable while native rows stay disabled. Pointer warmup now uses the actual backing density rather than 1. Both changes are checked at real 1x/2x and by the broad regression suite."
  ],
  "open": [
    "Shared list transport/owner validation/recovery and Chromium/Gecko listbox/multiple-select bindings, original DOM event/cancellation/default transactions and native intrinsic-layout integration.",
    "Broader row-model mutations, selection/scroll anchoring across reorder/removal, large lists, separators/group headers/rich rows, drag/autoscroll, accessibility, focus traversal, transforms/scaling and session-host recovery.",
    "Remaining browser controls, complete detached menus/native shortcuts, IME/accessibility, Chromium/Firefox derivatives and installed deployment; subsequent GTK/Qt/KDE integration via this same provider.",
    "Browser toolbar/address bar/tabs keep their existing components. Future requested changes remain optional app-specific patches above the shared bridge and UI library."
  ],
